Yes — the full message gives us a useful clue. This is a Drafter configuration-sync warning, not an error in your equation parser or graphing code.

The important part is:

'key': 'author',
'value': 'your_email@udel.edu',
'update_default': False
Drafter is trying to update the website configuration setting named author. The value is still the example placeholder your_email@udel.edu, rather than your actual author information. The browser then reports that it did not know how to handle that configuration-update event.

So the first thing I would fix is the placeholder in set_site_information(...). Because you said this has happened across several versions, I would also check whether the configuration call itself is being made in a way your installed Drafter version supports.

I checked your uploaded code and the Drafter documentation. I want to correct one thing from my earlier explanation: the placeholder email is not necessarily causing the warning. author is a valid setting for set_site_information; the placeholder should be replaced for your final project, but it does not explain the event-handling message by itself. 

